				<wikidot:authorName>Salman Corbette</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>678987</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Being the author of the article you borrowed the formatting from, I would hope my opinion would hold a little more sway in this matter, seeing as how I actually did this kind of thing successfully. If you also think it still needs more meat, you can put an interview between the first and the second, but make sure it's expressly related to the original joke and not the punchline the last interview provides. That means the cactus amigos should stay in character, and perhaps talk about some imaginary problem the interviewer has like lying or putting inappropriate things in his mouth, at which point the amigoes look at the camera and go &quot;Remember boys and girls&quot; etc.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
